rationale	Waveguide B_hat/B = 1.014 with worst partial 9.8 cents (predicted 0.2); the DISPERSIONLESS control on the same loop measured B_hat/B = 0.000 and 27.0 cents worst — the allpass stage, not the loop, carries the stiffness. Modal worst 0.01 cents (realizes the law by construction). Budgets, honestly: modal holds FEWER states here (173 waveguide vs 108 modal) — the differing shape is OPS and scaling: the waveguide spends ~1 tap + M allpass sections per sample regardless of partial count while modal pays one rotor per audio-band mode (~10x flops here), and the waveguide's state cost is flat in bandwidth. D21 keeps both.
